  "goodToKnow": "Der Schotter is gravel or crushed stone, for railway beds, paths and roads (die Schotterpiste is a gravel track). Schottergärten, front gardens covered in stones, have been banned in several states, such as Baden-Württemberg, because they harm insects and heat up cities. In slang, Schotter means cash, like Kohle, Knete or Kies. It has no plural."
